+/*
+ * Reporting is rate-limited separately from sampling, rather than the two
+ * being locked together as one period.
+ *
+ * The sensor is read every PAW32XX_SAMPLE_INTERVAL_MS so short direction
+ * changes are not averaged away, but a report is only emitted once
+ * PAW32XX_REPORT_INTERVAL_MS has elapsed since the last one, because
+ * producing faster than the negotiated BLE connection interval (measured
+ * 10-20ms) just backs up the HID queues and arrives stale.
+ *
+ * The check is on elapsed time at sample points, not a timer that sleeps
+ * until the deadline: whichever sample first crosses the threshold
+ * reports immediately, so rate limiting costs no added latency.
+ */
+#define PAW32XX_REPORT_INTERVAL_MS 10
 
